{"author":{"id":"f4e4dbe251fbd7519eab696986bae317e93a786739d6cebe9c4c1e89dd44e465"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793513529,"nonce":"Myk+m+s1NqQsy98ZueucMB7u8hY=","title":"M5: Meta and tactics v1, verification server, store v1, MSBuild task, CLI","message":"Parent epic: listed in a comment below. Depends on M4.\n\n\nThe first end-to-end developer experience: proofs are found by untrusted tactics, checked by the kernel, cached, and reported as build errors.\n\n- `LeanSharp.Meta` and tactics v1: `intro`, `exact`, `apply`, `cases`, `induction`, `simp`, `omega` (ported from Lean's `src/Lean/Meta/`, Ansatz as second reference).\n- `leansharp-server` (net10.0, design §8.1): JSON-RPC over named pipe / Unix socket; `verify`, `cancel`, `status`, `explain`, `export`, `report`; per-unit fuel and wall-clock limits.\n- Content-addressed cache (design §8.2) keyed on canonical VIR, dependency statements, bundle/environment hashes and kernel version; certificates can be re-checked by the kernel alone (`LeanSharpRecheck=true`).\n- Store v1 (design §7.3, moved here from M3): versioned binary format, content-addressed blobs, name index, memory-mapped reads, manifest. Includes trusted vs verified import modes (design §7.2).\n- `LeanSharp.Build` MSBuild task after `CoreCompile` (design §8.3), authoritative for builds and CI.\n- CLI grows `verify`, `check-store`, `import`, `explain` (design §3.2).\n- `LeanSharp.Analyzers`: deterministic checks only, no I/O.\n\n\nA false theorem fails the build with its goal shown.\n\nStatus: not started.","files":null}]}